description:
## Pipeline Failure

`MatchNarrationE2ETest.testPlayerCanSeeFeedbackInLeagueMatch:166` throws `NoSuchElementException` for `#feedback-area` in CI.

## Root Cause

### Participation check in MatchView (lines 608–618)

```java
boolean isParticipatingPlayer =
    isPlayerOnly
        && wrestlers.stream()
            .filter(Objects::nonNull)
            .anyMatch(w -> {
                Long accountId = securityUtils.getCurrentAccountId().orElse(null);
                return accountId \!= null
                    && w.getAccount() \!= null          // ← requires Wrestler.account to be set
                    && accountId.equals(w.getAccount().getId());
            });
boolean showFeedbackArea = isBookerOrAdmin || isParticipatingPlayer;
if (showFeedbackArea) {
    narrationContent.add(feedbackArea);   // only added if participating
}
```

`feedbackArea` is only added to the DOM when `isParticipatingPlayer` is true. That check requires the `Wrestler` entity to have its `account` field populated.

### Test setup (MatchNarrationE2ETest.java ~line 73–90)

The test creates `playerWrestler` and a `playerAccount`, links them via `Account.activeWrestlerId`:

```java
playerAccount.setActiveWrestlerId(playerWrestler.getId());  // account → wrestler
accountRepository.saveAndFlush(playerAccount);
// ← MISSING: playerWrestler.setAccount(playerAccount)
//             wrestlerService.save(playerWrestler)
```

The reverse relationship (`Wrestler.account`) is never set. So when MatchView loads `seg.getWrestlers()` and evaluates `w.getAccount()`, it returns `null` for the player wrestler, `isParticipatingPlayer` is `false`, and `feedbackArea` is never added to the DOM.

## Fix

In `MatchNarrationE2ETest.setupData()`, after saving `playerAccount`, set the account back on the wrestler and re-save:

```java
// Link wrestler → account (required for MatchView participation check)
Account savedAccount = accountRepository.findByUsername("player1").orElseThrow();
playerWrestler.setAccount(savedAccount);
wrestlerService.save(playerWrestler);
```

This must happen after the account is persisted so that a valid `Account` with an ID is set on the wrestler.

## Affected Files

| File | Line | Change |
|---|---|---|
| MatchNarrationE2ETest.java | ~89 (after playerAccount is saved) | Add `playerWrestler.setAccount(...); wrestlerService.save(playerWrestler);` |

## Test Verification

After the fix, `isParticipatingPlayer` resolves to `true` for `player1`, `feedbackArea` is present in the DOM, and `driver.findElement(By.id("feedback-area")).isDisplayed()` returns `true`.

## Bug

When opening the edit-segment dialog from Show Detail view, wrestlers are loaded one per row (each in their own team) instead of grouped by their saved `teamNumber`. The result is that editing any segment with pre-assigned teams (e.g. a tag team match) immediately scrambles the team layout in the UI; saving then overwrites the correct groupings with the broken one-wrestler-per-team layout, permanently destroying the team assignment.

## Steps to Reproduce

1. Create a tag team match segment with two teams (e.g. Team 1: Wrestler A + B, Team 2: Wrestler C + D)
2. Save the segment
3. Open Show Detail → click the edit button on that segment
4. Observe: the dialog shows 4 separate teams, each containing one wrestler
5. Click Save Changes without touching anything
6. Team assignments are now destroyed (each wrestler is their own team)

## Root Cause

**ShowDetailView.openEditSegmentDialog()** — line 1432–1433:

```java
// WRONG: iterates flat wrestler list, creates one team row per wrestler
for (Wrestler w : seg.getWrestlers()) {
    addTeamRow.accept(new HashSet<>(Set.of(w)));
}
```

`seg.getWrestlers()` returns all participants as a flat list with no team grouping. Each call to `addTeamRow` creates a brand-new team row containing just that one wrestler.

## Correct Approach (NarrationDialog — works)

**NarrationDialog** lines 242–263 uses `getWrestlersByTeam()` which returns a `Map<Integer, List<Wrestler>>` keyed by `SegmentParticipant.teamNumber`:

```java
Map<Integer, List<Wrestler>> byTeam = this.segment.getWrestlersByTeam();
if (byTeam.isEmpty()) {
    // legacy fallback: one row per wrestler
    wrestlerService.findAllBySegment(...).forEach(this::addTeamSelector);
} else {
    byTeam.forEach((teamNumber, wrestlers) -> addTeamSelector(dtos));
}
```

## Required Fix

In **ShowDetailView.openEditSegmentDialog()**, replace lines 1431–1438 with the same `getWrestlersByTeam()`-based grouping that NarrationDialog uses:

```java
// Group existing wrestlers by their saved teamNumber
Map<Integer, List<Wrestler>> byTeam = seg.getWrestlersByTeam();
if (byTeam.isEmpty()) {
    // Legacy fallback: one row per wrestler
    for (Wrestler w : seg.getWrestlers()) {
        addTeamRow.accept(new HashSet<>(Set.of(w)));
    }
} else {
    // Restore teams as saved
    byTeam.forEach((teamNumber, wrestlers) -> addTeamRow.accept(new HashSet<>(wrestlers)));
}
if (teamCombos.isEmpty()) {
    addTeamRow.accept(new HashSet<>());
    addTeamRow.accept(new HashSet<>());
}
```

Note: the `addTeamRow` consumer takes a `Set<Wrestler>`, so no type changes are needed — just pass `new HashSet<>(wrestlers)`.

## Affected Files

| File | Line | Change |
|---|---|---|
| ShowDetailView.java | 1431–1438 | Replace flat wrestler loop with `getWrestlersByTeam()` grouping |

## Test Coverage

Add or extend an integration/E2E test that:
1. Creates a segment with 2+ wrestlers assigned across 2 named teams
2. Opens the edit dialog
3. Saves without modifications
4. Verifies team assignments are unchanged in the database
